WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.833
(mysterious, whimsical music)

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.349
- [Narrator] In Northern Lithuania,

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:13.832
near the city of Siauliai,
hundreds of thousands

00:00:13.832 --> 00:00:15.915
of crosses sit on a hill.

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:23.112
Now representing both
the Lithuanian identity

00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:26.061
and Christian devotion,
this site of pilgrimage

00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:28.728
offers peace to those who visit.

00:00:30.013 --> 00:00:32.346
This is the Hill of Crosses.

00:00:35.521 --> 00:00:39.354
(mysterious, whimsical music)

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.543
The tradition of leaving
crosses began in 1831

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.010
to commemorate those who had fallen

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.510
in a rebellion against Russia.

00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:53.623
People still leave crosses today.

00:00:53.623 --> 00:00:57.456
(mysterious, whimsical music)

